; RP121032.ini lives in the Windows directory and lists every RP1210 driver installed on the
; machine. Applications read it to discover which adapters they can talk to.
;
; DO NOT overwrite an existing RP121032.ini: other vendors' drivers are listed in it. Add CANSUB32
; to the existing APIImplementations line instead, comma separated. tools\install.bat does this
; correctly; this file only shows the result.

[RP1210Support]
APIImplementations=CANSUB32
